30,2,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,The taster forms are clear. People are scared of a full-year commitment. We need flexibility.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The ledger confirms it. Seventy percent of our costs are fixed. The treasurer’s logs show individual chasing is a nightmare.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The data is stark. A quarter of us do two-thirds of the work. The rest are barely there.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,This confirms my fear. The door charge killed the vibe. People stopped feeling they belonged.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,The bank statements are worrying. A third needed reminders. We can’t rely on a single annual hit.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, if individual chasing is that bad, we must avoid activity-based charging. It’s too messy.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, exactly. A flat fee is the only way to keep the books sane. But it feels unfair to the absentees.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, it is unfair. But if we tier it, we create the friction Shunichi fears.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin"",""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, tiering might actually help. It lets people choose their level of involvement without guilt.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,I’m leaning toward a base fee. It covers the fixed costs. But we need to be careful with the extras.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"A base fee plus event charges? It’s transparent, but it might scare off the newcomers again.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,It’s the only way to balance the books without the administrative hell. I’m in.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I can live with it. It acknowledges that not everyone can do everything.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"If the base fee is low, it preserves the sense of belonging. The event charges are optional.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I agree. It’s not perfect, but it’s the most honest way to handle the fixed costs.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
