60,3,1,talk,Asuka,,Option C seems best. It protects the newcomers from a huge upfront cost.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,I’m with Asuka. Option A is too rigid. Option B creates social divides. C is practical.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,I’m hesitant. C might make the heavy users feel like they’re paying for the light users.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, the base fee covers the shared costs. The event fee is for the specific activity. It’s fair.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Takumi,,I’m voting C. It matches the cost to the usage. It’s the most logical solution.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shunichi, yes. And it avoids the administrative burden Benjamin is worried about.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Shunichi"",""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, the chasing is still there, but it’s per event, not per person. It’s manageable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I’ll go with C. It’s better than the alternatives.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,I’m voting C. It preserves the casual nature of the club.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
